  "chain": "pipe geometry/material design shortcoming [cause TBD] -> erosion of Al-Brz vent line -> pinhole through-wall leak -> ECW Train C inoperable (cascades ESF DG, RHR, CCW, CS, RCFC, CRE HVAC, ECCS); separately -> Essential Chiller 12B temp control loop malfunction (indeterminate cause) -> Essential Chilled Water Train B inoperable (cascades ECCS, CRE HVAC, CS, Electrical Penetrations HVAC) -> two of three safety trains inoperable simultaneously (47 min), condition could have prevented fulfillment of a safety function",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel, independent failure chains converge on the same reportable consequence (two-train inoperability window). Official cause_code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative gives a design/material erosion mechanism for ECW Train C and an explicitly indeterminate cause for Essential Chilled Water Train B (the temperature sensor/relay TCM damage findings came from later monitoring installed as a corrective action and were not confirmed as the cause of this specific event, so they are captured as related but not asserted in the causal chain). No backups are asserted since narrative does not state an operable/available backup system during the two-train inoperable window (in fact this is the reportable condition itself: only one train remained). Previous-occurrence LER keys copied exactly as stated in narrative (no leading unit digit given in source text)."
